
Interpreter variables: x, y, z, etc except s which is reserved for the audio server.
    s.boot; s.quit;

Environment variables which *always* begin with a tilde when declared or used.
    ~myVariable = 10;
    ~myVariable.postln;

Local variables within a block statement: they are only local to the block itself.
    (var hello = "Hello";
     hello.postln);

Function arguments.
    { arg x, y;
      x+y}
or
    {|x, y|; x+y}

User-defined classes: 
    Foo


~arr = [1, 2, 3, 4];
~arr = (1..4);
~arr = Array.series(1, 4, 1);
~arr = (1,1..4)

~arr.at(index);
~arr.index;

~arr = Array.series(1,100,1);
~arr = Array.geom(1,12,~twelfthRoot2);

